WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
The Pilbara, in Australia.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.590
Here, iron ore is dug from open pits.

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.250
One company's ore trains run on
nearly 2,000 kilometres of railway,

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.610
out to four port terminals.

5
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.890
In 2025, Australia mined 980
million tonnes of usable ore.

6
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.630
Brazil mined 420 million.

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:27.310
Together, that is over half of
the world's 2,600 million tonnes.

8
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.770
Why do just two countries dominate?

9
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.830
And where does all that ore go?

10
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.750
In this mission, you'll find
out what iron ore is for,

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.230
and what drives demand for it.

12
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.470
Then you'll read the
rocks that hold the ore,

13
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.270
and trace where the ships sail.

14
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.610
Your mission: explain why two countries
mine over half the world's iron ore,

15
00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.040
and who buys it.
